        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It seems that real-time shadows were never meant to be enabled on Quest!\nOculus [strongly recommends against](https://developer.oculus.com/blog/pc-rendering-techniques-to-avoid-when-developing-for-mobile-vr/) several things on Quest, and realtime shadows is one of them. \nOculus basically recommends against everything in the statement given here: \"shadows no longer show with realtime lights when using Unity standard shaders in a Quest world\"\n- Unity Standard is expensive, which is why it's not on our \"supported\" shaders list. You *really* shouldn't use Standard on Quest worlds, use Baked. Standard Lite if you must.\n- Real-time lighting is expensive, which is why Quest was originally limited to 1 real-time pixel shaded light. This was missed thanks to some odd Unity behavior when adjusting settings profiles.\n- Shadows are *extra* expensive, so they were disabled.\nThat being said, it was enabled for quite some time so people may have gotten used to it.\nWe're not making any changes yet but we're investigating our alternatives here.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-06T21:47:53.237Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Ever since the Unity 2019 upgrade, objects no longer cast shadows behind realtime lights when using Unity standard shaders in a Quest world. This happens even after re-uploading with the new editor.",
